// Castellum - DEVELOPMENT (Debug configuration) build settings.
//
// Ad-hoc signed, so a local build and the unsigned CI job need no certificate
// and no keychain access (an Apple Development identity would make every
// agent build hit a codesign keychain prompt instead).
//
// Dev/prod identity split (2026-09-23). A Debug build is a DIFFERENT app to
// macOS: bundle id uk.co.riera.castellum.dev, shown as "Castellum Dev". TCC
// records grants per bundle id, and an ad-hoc signature changes with every
// build, so sharing the production id meant every one of ~120 DerivedData
// copies polluted the shipped app's Privacy & Security rows (Contacts,
// Calendars, App Data). Keeping the file/executable name "Castellum.app"
// (PRODUCT_NAME) is deliberate: scripts, skills and TEST_HOST all find the
// app by that path. The profile directory and Keychain namespaces are NOT
// keyed on the bundle id, so the dev build still opens the same mail profile.

CASTELLUM_BUNDLE_ID_SUFFIX = .dev
CASTELLUM_DISPLAY_NAME = Castellum Dev

CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = Castellum.entitlements
ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME = YES
// Empty => $(TeamIdentifierPrefix) is empty, so the App Group entitlement
// expands to a bare id that SharePendingCompose refuses to open (no Team ID
// can authorize it): the Share Extension handoff is off in Debug by design,
// which is what keeps Debug builds from raising the App Data prompt.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

